==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|abevarn}}, from {{inh|de|goh|abafaran}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*abafaran}}. Equivalent to {{prefix|de|ab|fahren|t1=from|t2=drive}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|afvaren}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|[ˈapfaːrən]}}
* {{audio|de|De-abfahren.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-abfahren2.ogg}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-abfahren.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{hyphenation|de|ab|fah|ren}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb|ab.fahren<fährt#fuhr,gefahren,führe.haben,sein>}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[depart]], to [[leave]] {{+aux|de|sein}}
#: {{ux|de|Ihr Zug '''fährt''' um fünf Uhr '''ab.'''|Her train departs at 5 o'clock.}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir werden morgen '''abfahren.'''|We will '''leave''' tomorrow}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[carry off]], to [[remove]] {{+aux|de|haben}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Müll wird zweimal pro Woche '''abgefahren'''.|The garbage is '''picked up''' twice a week.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|idiomatic|colloquial}} to [[go for]]; to be [[crazy]] about, for; to be a [[fan]] of or [[infatuated]] with {{+obj|de|:auf<someone/something>}} {{+aux|de|sein}}
#: {{ux|de|Sie '''fährt''' voll auf Kultfilme '''ab.'''|She''''s''' really '''crazy about''' cult movies.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[drive]] [[along]] {{q|a stretch of road in search of something}}; to [[patrol]] {{+aux|de|sein|haben}}
#: {{ux|de|
Lass uns die Strecke noch mal '''abfahren''', vielleicht finden wir ihn doch.|Let's '''drive along''' this stretch of road again, we might still find him}}
# to [[wear down]] (tyres/tires)
# to [[use up]] (all one's journeys on a travel card)
# to [[knock off]] (something by hitting it with one's vehicle)
# {{lb|de|jemanden abfahren lassen|vulgar}} to send someone packing; to tell someone to go away

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj|ab.fahren<fährt#fuhr,gefahren,führe.haben,sein>}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|de|abreisen}}
* auf etw. {{l|de|stehen}}

